BILLAS INTRODUCED AND PASSED BY SENATE S.181
2026 Page 1 of 6
1 S.181
2 Introduced by Senator Hashim
3 Referred to Committee on Judiciary
4 Date: January 6, 2026
5 Subject: Crimes and criminal procedure; sentencing; deferred sentence
6 Statement of purpose of bill as introduced: This bill proposes to eliminate the
7 requirement that a presentence investigation is filed with the court prior to the
8 court imposing a deferred sentence.
9 An act relating to eliminating the requirement for a presentence
10 investigation for imposition of a deferred sentence
11 It is hereby enacted by the General Assembly of the State of Vermont:
12 Sec. 1. 13 V.S.A. § 7041 is amended to read:
13 § 7041. DEFERRED SENTENCE
14 (a) Upon an adjudication of guilt and after the filing of a presentence
15 investigation report, the court may defer sentencing and place the respondent
16 on probation upon such terms and conditions as it may require if a written
17 agreement concerning the deferring of sentence is entered into between the
18 State’s Attorney and the respondent and filed with the clerk of the court.
19 (b) Notwithstanding subsection (a) of this section, the court may defer
20 sentencing and place the respondent on probation without a written agreement

